 Outstanding evidence

Executive summary

RaceDay is a role-based event management and results tracking application
developed with ASP.NET Core and .NET 8. It combines a RESTful Web API, an
ASP.NET Core MVC web client, a SQL Server relational database, and Azure Blob
Storage for event banners and profile pictures. The platform serves two user groups:
participants, who discover events, enrol and view their results; and organisers, who
create and administer events, categories, participants and results.

The solution demonstrates separation of concerns through API, MVC, shared
contracts and automated test projects. Authentication and authorisation restrict
functionality by role and event ownership. Entity Framework Core supports relational
persistence, while GitHub Actions provides continuous integration. The final API and
MVC images were built with Docker, tested locally and pushed to Docker Hub on 6
November 2026.

Evidence reviewed for this report includes a successful HTTP 200 response from the
containerised events API; successful participant and organiser logins and working
dashboards; a passing Release build and four passing unit tests; successful GitHub
Actions execution; and successful Docker Hub image publication. This report
documents implemented functionality and limitations without presenting the system
as publicly hosted or the pending demonstration video as completed.
