13.2 Build process

Both applications were packaged using .NET 8 multi-stage Dockerfiles. The build
stage restored project dependencies and published Release output; the runtime
stage used the ASP.NET Core 8 image to run the application. Docker image
inspection showed port 8080 exposed for the API and ports 8080 and 8081 for the
MVC image. Images were built from the solution root and tagged under the
developer’s Docker Hub account.

                                                                                 9
13.3 Runtime testing and troubleshooting

The API container was mapped from host port 7009 to container port 8080. Its first
request returned HTTP 500 because AzureStorage:ConnectionString was not
configured in the container. After providing Azure storage settings, a second HTTP
500 identified an uninitialised SQL Server connection string. The developer
confirmed the SQL Server service and database, enabled a dedicated SQL login,
and supplied a container-compatible connection string. A subsequent GET
/api/events returned HTTP 200.

The MVC container was accessible at localhost:7010. The landing page, login,
participant dashboard, enrolment list, organiser dashboard, My Events and All
Events were demonstrated successfully. Finally, both images were pushed to Docker
Hub and their updated repository pages were shown.

13.4 Deployment status

Deployment status: local Docker deployment verified and Docker Hub image
publication completed on 6 November 2026. This does not constitute a production
cloud deployment or an internet-accessible hosted application. The image
repositories enable future deployment to an appropriate container hosting
environment.

